WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.780
Module 5: the Leadership Mosaic 360.

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:06.718
The Culture Mosaic shows
how an organization works.

00:00:06.718 --> 00:00:13.049
The Leadership Mosaic 360 shows how one
leader is experienced by the people around

00:00:13.049 --> 00:00:16.987
them, their boss, peers,
direct reports and others,

00:00:16.987 --> 00:00:21.079
and sets that against how
the leader sees themselves.

00:00:21.079 --> 00:00:22.469
A 360 is personal.

00:00:22.469 --> 00:00:28.724
Done well, it's one of the most useful
development experiences a leader ever has.

00:00:28.724 --> 00:00:31.735
Done carelessly, it damages trust fast.

00:00:31.735 --> 00:00:34.978
This module takes about a hundred minutes.

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:38.934
The Leadership Mosaic uses
the same four dimensions,

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:41.067
but it's a different instrument.

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:44.534
There are fifty-seven items
on a one-to-seven scale.

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:49.335
Raters can skip an item, and a skipped
item is left out of the averages,

00:00:49.335 --> 00:00:50.802
never counted as zero.

00:00:50.802 --> 00:00:55.135
There are three open questions:
what strengths the leader brings,

00:00:55.135 --> 00:00:59.202
where they can improve, and what
their biggest blind spot is.

00:00:59.202 --> 00:01:04.670
It takes a rater about fifteen to twenty
minutes, in any of twenty-nine languages.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:08.270
The twelve tiles are the same
as the Culture Mosaic's,

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:11.537
Customer under Adapt and
Decisions under Deliver.

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:16.871
The items are locked, to keep the comparison
with the benchmark pool of leaders.

00:01:16.871 --> 00:01:21.671
And never compare a one-to-seven
Leadership Mosaic score directly with a

00:01:21.671 --> 00:01:23.872
one-to-five Culture Mosaic score.

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:26.650
Every item comes in two versions.

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:32.325
The leader answers in the first person: "I
create space for others to contribute."

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:34.678
Raters answer in the third person,

00:01:34.678 --> 00:01:40.075
with the leader's name: "Jordan Reyes
creates space for others to contribute."

00:01:40.075 --> 00:01:42.636
Because both rate the same behaviour,

00:01:42.636 --> 00:01:46.926
the report can set how I see
myself next to how others see me.

00:01:46.926 --> 00:01:50.594
That comparison is where
most of a 360's value lives.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:54.979
How a 360 is framed decides
how honestly people answer.

00:01:54.979 --> 00:01:58.505
Say this: the 360 is for
the leader's development.

00:01:58.505 --> 00:02:00.551
It's a mirror, not a verdict.

00:02:00.551 --> 00:02:06.404
Never let it feed a performance rating,
pay, promotion or a restructuring decision.

00:02:06.404 --> 00:02:12.188
Raters who suspect their answers could cost
someone a job either soften everything

00:02:12.188 --> 00:02:13.880
or don't respond at all.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:17.477
Before launch, agree three
things with the sponsor.

00:02:17.477 --> 00:02:23.119
Who sees the report: usually the leader
and their coach or debrief practitioner,

00:02:23.119 --> 00:02:27.562
and anyone beyond that should be
agreed and told to the leader.

00:02:27.562 --> 00:02:32.358
What happens next: a debrief and a
development plan the leader owns.

00:02:32.358 --> 00:02:37.295
And what the invitation says about
why the organization is running it.

00:02:37.295 --> 00:02:42.796
If a sponsor says "we'll use this in the
talent review", stop and renegotiate.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:47.995
A Leadership Mosaic is bought as one
seat per leader receiving feedback.

00:02:47.995 --> 00:02:50.017
Raters are never charged extra.

00:02:50.017 --> 00:02:54.320
When you assign a seat, you choose
"for me" or "for someone else",

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:59.733
and SurveyCraft copies the Leadership Mosaic
master into the client's organization,

00:02:59.733 --> 00:03:02.733
with protections on and
every question locked.

00:03:02.733 --> 00:03:07.102
The leader gets a personal portal
with their self-assessment ready.

00:03:07.102 --> 00:03:09.840
Unassigned seats wait until you need them.

00:03:10.333 --> 00:03:12.638
The guided setup has six steps.

00:03:12.638 --> 00:03:14.868
Questions: the locked battery,

00:03:14.868 --> 00:03:19.031
plus any extra free-response
questions that were bought.

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:22.302
Participant workflow,
which you'll see next.

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:25.648
Participants: the leaders
receiving feedback.

00:03:25.648 --> 00:03:29.068
Raters, only if you're
managing them yourself.

00:03:29.068 --> 00:03:32.859
Invitation emails, where
you must approve the copy,

00:03:32.859 --> 00:03:37.766
so make sure it says the 360 is
for development and who sees what.

00:03:37.766 --> 00:03:39.401
And review and launch.

00:03:39.401 --> 00:03:43.862
Each extra question gets its
own pages in the leader's deck,

00:03:43.862 --> 00:03:48.694
after the blind-spot pages, with
the usual confidentiality rules.

00:03:48.694 --> 00:03:52.337
On timing: set a deadline
two to three weeks out.

00:03:52.337 --> 00:03:57.615
A reminder about a week in typically
drives a large share of responses.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.706
There are two workflows.

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:05.061
In the Standard workflow, the leader
nominates their own raters in their portal.

00:04:05.061 --> 00:04:09.076
It works best when leaders know
their working relationships,

00:04:09.076 --> 00:04:14.230
and ownership matters for development,
but coach them to pick a balanced mix.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:18.246
In the Self-assessment-only
workflow, you manage the raters,

00:04:18.246 --> 00:04:23.533
which gives a consistent design but needs
accurate rater lists from the client.

00:04:23.533 --> 00:04:26.746
Most development 360s use
the Standard workflow,

00:04:26.746 --> 00:04:30.962
because owning the rater list
helps the leader own the results.

00:04:31.467 --> 00:04:34.105
The leader's portal has three steps.

00:04:34.105 --> 00:04:36.083
First, the self-assessment.

00:04:36.083 --> 00:04:41.652
Encourage leaders to do it first, before
they've heard anything from raters.

00:04:41.652 --> 00:04:47.734
Second, invite raters, by name, email and
role: boss, peer, direct report or other.

00:04:47.734 --> 00:04:51.031
Each rater gets a
confidential personal link.

00:04:51.031 --> 00:04:52.716
Third, track responses.

00:04:52.716 --> 00:04:55.721
The portal shows how many have responded,

00:04:55.721 --> 00:04:59.458
but names and individual
answers stay confidential,

00:04:59.458 --> 00:05:03.634
and the leader can remind
pending raters with one button.

00:05:03.634 --> 00:05:09.570
Once raters have responded, the administrator
generates the report and shares it,

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:12.061
ideally in a debrief conversation.

00:05:12.567 --> 00:05:18.017
The single biggest lever on 360 response
rates is a personal note from the leader

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:20.036
before the invitations arrive.

00:05:20.036 --> 00:05:22.459
The portal offers a ready-made note.

00:05:22.459 --> 00:05:27.640
The leader edits it and sends it from
their own email, with addresses in Bcc,

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:30.736
a day or two before
pressing Send Invitations.

00:05:30.736 --> 00:05:34.370
Then they mark "I've sent
it", so you can see it went.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:39.619
The note asks raters to be candid and
says it takes fifteen to twenty minutes.

00:05:39.619 --> 00:05:45.070
Coach the leader to add one sentence of
their own: "I'm doing this because I want

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:47.559
to get better at" something specific.

00:05:47.559 --> 00:05:49.713
Genuine curiosity is contagious.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.918
Every rater belongs to one category.

00:05:52.918 --> 00:05:54.353
Self is the leader.

00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:59.941
Boss is the person or people they report
to, and in the individual report,

00:05:59.941 --> 00:06:02.055
bosses are named, up to two.

00:06:02.055 --> 00:06:06.510
Peers, direct reports and others
are grouped and anonymous,

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:09.531
and each needs at least three responses.

00:06:09.531 --> 00:06:15.270
The report also shows "All Others":
every rater except the leader, combined.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:18.517
That's the main "how
others see me" figure.

00:06:19.033 --> 00:06:22.867
Here's how the Leadership
Mosaic protects small groups.

00:06:22.867 --> 00:06:28.654
Peers, direct reports and others each need
at least three completed responses to be

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:29.072
shown.

00:06:29.072 --> 00:06:32.627
If a category falls short,
its columns show a dash,

00:06:32.627 --> 00:06:37.437
and its raters go into a shared pool
with any other short categories.

00:06:37.437 --> 00:06:41.550
If that pool reaches three,
they still count in All Others.

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:45.315
If it doesn't, they're left
out of All Others as well,

00:06:45.315 --> 00:06:50.961
because otherwise you could subtract the
visible groups and work out exactly what

00:06:50.961 --> 00:06:52.216
those people said.

00:06:52.216 --> 00:06:55.004
Either way, their comments are withheld.

00:06:55.004 --> 00:06:58.629
In Jordan Reyes's 360, two
"Other" raters responded.

00:06:58.629 --> 00:07:01.697
Two is fewer than three,
so Other is hidden,

00:07:01.697 --> 00:07:05.182
and those two are left out
of All Others entirely.

00:07:05.182 --> 00:07:10.411
All Others is the boss, four peers and
seven direct reports: twelve raters.

00:07:10.411 --> 00:07:12.572
Self and Boss are never folded.

00:07:12.572 --> 00:07:17.939
The threshold is three, and an organization
can raise it, but never lower it.

00:07:18.433 --> 00:07:19.599
Here's the rule.

00:07:19.599 --> 00:07:25.717
In the individual report, boss feedback is
attributed by name, as Boss 1 and Boss 2.

00:07:25.717 --> 00:07:31.763
A leader already knows who they report to,
and naming it keeps the feedback useful.

00:07:31.763 --> 00:07:36.351
At most two bosses are named,
and the leader chooses which two.

00:07:36.351 --> 00:07:39.993
Any other boss is counted
anonymously with Others,

00:07:39.993 --> 00:07:44.874
and the portal tags each boss so
the leader can see which is which.

00:07:44.874 --> 00:07:48.443
Peers, direct reports and
others are never named.

00:07:48.443 --> 00:07:53.687
Before launch, tell the leader that
boss feedback will be shown by name.

00:07:53.687 --> 00:07:56.965
Make sure each boss
knows before they answer.

00:07:56.965 --> 00:08:02.646
And if the leader has three or more
bosses, agree which two are rated as Boss.

00:08:02.646 --> 00:08:05.997
The product tells bosses,
in their invitation,

00:08:05.997 --> 00:08:09.274
on the consent screen
and on the survey page,

00:08:09.274 --> 00:08:15.247
that their name appears next to their
feedback and that up to two boss ratings are

00:08:15.247 --> 00:08:16.631
identified by name.

00:08:16.631 --> 00:08:19.763
That's not a substitute
for a conversation.

00:08:19.763 --> 00:08:22.094
Make sure they hear it from you.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:25.544
A 360 is only as good as its rater list.

00:08:25.544 --> 00:08:27.753
Coach leaders on three things.

00:08:27.753 --> 00:08:33.715
Numbers: at least three per category they
care about, and five to seven is ideal,

00:08:33.715 --> 00:08:35.703
to allow for non-responses.

00:08:35.703 --> 00:08:41.812
Balance: people who see the leader's work
regularly, not just people who like them,

00:08:41.812 --> 00:08:45.272
including someone the
leader finds challenging.

00:08:45.272 --> 00:08:47.480
And bosses: one or two, named.

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:50.866
Jordan invited five peers,
and four responded.

00:08:50.866 --> 00:08:53.958
Eight direct reports, and seven responded.

00:08:53.958 --> 00:08:59.479
But inviting only two "Other" raters
guaranteed that group would be hidden.

00:08:59.479 --> 00:09:03.969
To get the board's view, Jordan
needed at least three others,

00:09:03.969 --> 00:09:06.251
and realistically four or five.

00:09:06.767 --> 00:09:12.685
Leaders can remind pending raters from
their portal, admins can resend invitations,

00:09:12.685 --> 00:09:17.533
and you can set automatic reminders
every three, five or seven days.

00:09:17.533 --> 00:09:20.742
They go only to raters
who haven't completed.

00:09:20.742 --> 00:09:26.446
Owners and admins get a readiness email
for each leader once every invited rater

00:09:26.446 --> 00:09:28.443
group has three completions.

00:09:28.443 --> 00:09:31.865
That's your signal the
report has what it needs.

00:09:31.865 --> 00:09:34.004
You close feedback per leader.

00:09:34.004 --> 00:09:39.566
Once closed, that leader's raters can't
submit and no new raters can be added,

00:09:39.566 --> 00:09:41.776
and closing unlocks the report.

00:09:41.776 --> 00:09:43.416
Treat closing as final.

00:09:43.933 --> 00:09:48.441
To generate a report, open the 360
project, find the leader's row,

00:09:48.441 --> 00:09:49.738
and press Download.

00:09:49.738 --> 00:09:52.743
The designed PowerPoint
is built in seconds.

00:09:52.743 --> 00:09:55.885
Then share it in a
conversation, not an inbox.

00:09:55.885 --> 00:09:57.729
And generate after closing.

00:09:57.729 --> 00:10:02.510
If you generate before the leader's
feedback closes, the report works,

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:05.719
but the leader doesn't
join the benchmark pool.

00:10:06.233 --> 00:10:09.121
Let's walk through Jordan Reyes's report.

00:10:09.121 --> 00:10:13.559
After the framework pages, each
item gets a row for Self, Boss,

00:10:13.559 --> 00:10:18.912
Peers and Direct Reports: the average,
the percentile against other leaders,

00:10:18.912 --> 00:10:20.954
and how many people answered.

00:10:20.954 --> 00:10:25.321
The grey band shows the typical
range for leaders in the pool.

00:10:25.321 --> 00:10:30.675
Next, heatmaps colour each item's
percentile by group, so patterns jump out.

00:10:30.675 --> 00:10:36.521
Then the comparison mosaics, one diamond
per group, with tiles sized by percentile,

00:10:36.521 --> 00:10:42.156
so you can see at a glance where Jordan's
direct reports see something different

00:10:42.156 --> 00:10:43.001
from Jordan.

00:10:43.001 --> 00:10:47.720
Finally, the comments: a summary
for each rater group on strengths,

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:49.692
improvement and blind spots.

00:10:49.692 --> 00:10:52.862
You'll learn to read
all of this in Module 8.

00:10:53.367 --> 00:10:55.948
Don't promise pages that aren't there.

00:10:55.948 --> 00:10:59.278
There's no blind-spots or
hidden-strengths slide.

00:10:59.278 --> 00:11:04.917
You find those yourself, by comparing Self
with others, and Module 8 shows you how.

00:11:04.917 --> 00:11:07.635
There's no top-five or bottom-five list.

00:11:07.635 --> 00:11:10.420
"Other" raters don't get item-level rows.

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:14.089
Comments from folded categories
are withheld entirely.

00:11:14.089 --> 00:11:18.641
And the third open question asks
raters about a biggest blind spot.

00:11:18.641 --> 00:11:22.990
That's their view in their own
words, not a calculated analysis.

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:29.147
By default, a leader joins the Leadership
Mosaic benchmark pool when their report

00:11:29.147 --> 00:11:32.284
is generated after their
feedback has closed.

00:11:32.284 --> 00:11:37.651
They stay out if the organization switched
off the benchmark on the 360 page,

00:11:37.651 --> 00:11:43.437
the buyer declined consent, it's an internal
account, or any response is test data.

00:11:43.437 --> 00:11:48.596
Percentiles need at least thirty leaders
in the pool, or they show a dash.

00:11:48.596 --> 00:11:54.382
On retention: raters' identifiable data is
kept for sixty days, then de-identified.

00:11:54.382 --> 00:11:59.331
The stored report is also kept for
sixty days, because it names bosses,

00:11:59.331 --> 00:12:04.769
and a copy with boss names removed is
kept so the leader can ask for it later.

00:12:04.769 --> 00:12:08.254
So download the report,
deliver it in the debrief,

00:12:08.254 --> 00:12:11.461
and make sure the leader
saves their own copy.

00:12:11.967 --> 00:12:17.644
The Team Report combines three to
twenty-five leaders' 360s into one view of a

00:12:17.644 --> 00:12:18.808
leadership team.

00:12:18.808 --> 00:12:23.175
Each leader must have a closed
360 in the same organization,

00:12:23.175 --> 00:12:28.852
with at least one completed rater, and
membership can't change after purchase.

00:12:28.852 --> 00:12:34.311
Bars show the equal-weight team mean,
the average of each leader's average,

00:12:34.311 --> 00:12:38.896
so a leader with twenty raters
counts the same as one with six.

00:12:38.896 --> 00:12:41.808
The band shows the range across leaders.

00:12:41.808 --> 00:12:46.684
Percentiles are the average of the
leaders' individual percentiles.

00:12:46.684 --> 00:12:49.377
The "Team Score" replaces All Others,

00:12:49.377 --> 00:12:54.035
and Self appears only if three or
more leaders rated themselves.

00:12:54.035 --> 00:12:55.564
People are protected.

00:12:55.564 --> 00:12:59.567
Bosses become one pooled,
anonymous group, never named.

00:12:59.567 --> 00:13:04.007
Every rater group needs three
or more raters across the team.

00:13:04.007 --> 00:13:07.209
There are no verbatim
comments, only themes.

00:13:07.209 --> 00:13:12.231
And "Where Each Leader Stands" shows
each leader as an unlabeled dot.

00:13:12.231 --> 00:13:18.199
At Northwind, the dots on Empowered Teams
range from three point six to five point

00:13:18.199 --> 00:13:19.873
seven, an uneven bench.

00:13:19.873 --> 00:13:22.785
Don't try to work out which dot is whom.

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:27.104
Here are the two reports
side by side: how the bars,

00:13:27.104 --> 00:13:31.860
bands and percentiles are calculated,
how bosses and Self appear,

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:33.981
and how comments are handled.

00:13:33.981 --> 00:13:38.591
One warning above all: never use
a Team Report to rank leaders.

00:13:38.591 --> 00:13:44.443
It's built so that you can't, and trying
undermines the trust that made the 360s

00:13:44.443 --> 00:13:44.956
honest.

00:13:45.467 --> 00:13:51.014
Coaches in Mosaic Coaching Studio can
deploy a 360 straight from a coaching

00:13:51.014 --> 00:13:51.827
engagement.

00:13:51.827 --> 00:13:55.526
It uses the same locked
items and the same report,

00:13:55.526 --> 00:13:59.668
it launches immediately with
the coach named as sponsor,

00:13:59.668 --> 00:14:03.809
and the coach retrieves the
report from Coaching Studio.

00:14:03.809 --> 00:14:09.431
Every rule in this module still applies:
the three-rater fold, named bosses,

00:14:09.431 --> 00:14:12.981
the heads-up note, and
closing before reporting.

00:14:12.981 --> 00:14:18.972
There's no Close button in Coaching Studio:
a Mosaic administrator closes the 360

00:14:18.972 --> 00:14:23.632
in SurveyCraft, so agree the end
date with your Mosaic contact.

00:14:24.133 --> 00:14:25.480
Now it's your turn.

00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:31.008
Northwind's CEO wants a 360 for Jordan
Reyes, the COO leading the integration.

00:14:31.008 --> 00:14:32.709
You're the practitioner.

00:14:32.709 --> 00:14:38.592
Work through eight decisions, from the
purpose of the 360 to closing and reporting.

00:14:38.592 --> 00:14:42.419
Some choices are critical
errors that end the attempt.

00:14:42.933 --> 00:14:47.295
Time for the module check: twelve
questions, and you need ten right.

00:14:47.295 --> 00:14:48.706
Retakes are unlimited.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:54.827
Here's your Leadership Mosaic 360 Setup
Checklist, including the Team Report.

00:14:54.827 --> 00:14:55.704
Download it.

00:14:56.200 --> 00:15:00.439
And here's a talk track for the
boss-attribution conversation.

00:15:00.439 --> 00:15:02.284
Use it before every launch.

00:15:02.284 --> 00:15:07.890
With the leader, explain that peers, direct
reports and others are always grouped,

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:12.129
but their boss's ratings and
comments appear under their name,

00:15:12.129 --> 00:15:15.410
and that you'll pick at
most two people as Boss.

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:19.717
With each boss, say clearly that
boss feedback isn't anonymous,

00:15:19.717 --> 00:15:24.912
and ask them to answer as candidly as
they would in a one-to-one development

00:15:24.912 --> 00:15:25.801
conversation.

00:15:25.801 --> 00:15:29.424
The card also covers what
to say if someone asks why,

00:15:29.424 --> 00:15:31.544
or would rather stay anonymous.

00:15:32.033 --> 00:15:32.713
To recap.

00:15:32.713 --> 00:15:38.907
The Leadership Mosaic has fifty-seven items
on a one-to-seven scale and three open

00:15:38.907 --> 00:15:43.289
questions, on the same twelve
tiles as the Culture Mosaic.

00:15:43.289 --> 00:15:46.461
Frame it as development, never evaluation.

00:15:46.461 --> 00:15:52.353
Bosses are named, two at most, so tell
the leader and each boss before launch.

00:15:52.353 --> 00:15:56.659
Peers, direct reports and
others each need three to show,

00:15:56.659 --> 00:15:59.152
and folded comments are withheld.

00:15:59.152 --> 00:16:03.911
Self-assessment first, heads-up
note second, invitations third.

00:16:03.911 --> 00:16:06.328
Close per leader, then generate.

00:16:06.328 --> 00:16:09.727
And the Team Report
pools bosses anonymously,

00:16:09.727 --> 00:16:12.824
has no verbatims and no labelled leaders.

00:16:12.824 --> 00:16:14.410
Never use it to rank.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:16.677
